        "evidence_id": "E20",
        "quote": "gaps remain persistently high in many sectors, with the average hourly median pay gap being 11.28% in 2024-25, a small reduction from the previous year."
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Flexible working can help carers, parents, and those with health conditions remain in employment, potentially broadening access to work for lower-paid groups.",
        "evidence_id": "E33",
        "quote": "This can be \"life-changing\" for millions, including parents, carers, and individuals with long-term health conditions, enabling them to remain in or access employment."
